  "section_notes": "S2 is the weakened section: a 7% permanent ceiling sits above the 5% threshold, and exceeding it triggers only corrective action with no sales stop, which favours Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%). S5 keeps the 8-per-100,000 mandatory recall trigger with no transition, which would capture Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9), while S4's 36-month suppression deadline favours Halcyon's cost position. S3's 6-year retrofit deadline sits within the acceptable range and favours Northwind, whose installed base is only 38% shut-off capable."
